# Optional: default AI provider baked into the one-click macOS installer
# (scripts/build-mac-installer.sh / scripts/package-mac-installer.sh).
#
# Quick start:
# 1) Copy this file to `installer.env` at the repo root.
# 2) Fill in the values below.
# 3) Keep real secrets out of git -- installer.env is gitignored.
#
# What this does: if installer.env exists when the installer is built, its
# values are baked in PLAINTEXT into the installer app bundle's Resources
# and used to finish `openclaw onboard` on the end user's Mac with a working
# model already configured -- they land straight in the chat window instead
# of OpenClaw.app's own first-run "pick a model" screen.
#
# This is meant for a SHARED default backend you are comfortable handing to
# everyone who receives the installer built from it (e.g. an internal vLLM
# endpoint), not a personal API key. Anyone who unzips/inspects the built
# .app can read these values back out in plain text.
#
# Leave this file absent (the default) to skip this entirely: the installer
# still does everything else non-interactively, and the end user just picks
# a provider themselves in OpenClaw.app, same as installing it normally.
#
# These are separate from this repo's own .env (used by the gateway/CLI at
# runtime when run from source) so the two never mix.

OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_PROVIDER=vllm
OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_MODEL=your-model-id
OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_API_KEY=

# Optional local-model (llama.cpp) fallback: a HuggingFace repo id, bundled
# at build time (a prebuilt llama-server binary for this build's arch --
# see scripts/build-mac-installer.sh) and downloaded from HuggingFace at
# first launch. Registered as a *backup* model once it's running --
# --custom-as-backup on `openclaw onboard` -- it never replaces the
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_* model above. Leave this absent to skip
# the whole feature (no binary bundled, nothing downloaded). Without a
# pinned file, the newest release's most-preferred quantization is
# auto-selected from the repo; pin one explicitly with "repo:filename.gguf",
# e.g. Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct-GGUF:qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_LLAMA_MODEL=unsloth/Qwen3.5-2B-GGUF:Qwen3.5-2B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# Leave unset for memory-aware selection: 32768 normally, or the model-native
# context when more than 10 GiB is available. Set 0 to force model-native.
# OPENCLAW_LLAMA_FALLBACK_CTX=32768

# Memory footprint of the local fallback server. llama-server's own defaults
# suit a dedicated inference box, not a fallback model sharing a 16 GB laptop:
# --cache-ram is 8192 MiB of host-RAM prompt cache that fills up over time, and
# -np is auto (several slots). The values below are what the setup script uses
# when these stay unset -- uncomment only to build an installer with different
# ones. Each also accepts "off" to pass no flag at all, and can be overridden
# at runtime by the matching OPENCLAW_LLAMA_FALLBACK_* environment variable.
# Do not set CACHE_RAM to 0: --kv-unified "requires cache-ram", so 0 would also
# disable the unified KV buffer (the setup script clamps it to 64 MiB).
# OPENCLAW_LLAMA_FALLBACK_CACHE_RAM=512   # MiB of host-RAM prompt cache
# OPENCLAW_LLAMA_FALLBACK_KV_TYPE=q8_0    # -ctk/-ctv; f16 is llama-server's default
# OPENCLAW_LLAMA_FALLBACK_SLOTS=1         # -np server slots
OPENCLAW_LLAMA_VERSION=b11149

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local AI modes (scripts/mac-local-ai-setup.sh, run in the background on
# every app launch). There is one local model: the small llama.cpp model
# above, which fits 8-16 GB Macs.
#
#   hybrid   OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ENABLE_LITELLM=1: adds the model
#            "Adaptive" (litellm-router/adaptive, a local LiteLLM
#            proxy on 127.0.0.1) and makes it the default. The local model reads
#            each request and classifies it SIMPLE / MEDIUM / COMPLEX /
#            REASONING; SIMPLE requests it answers itself, the others go to
#            models OpenClaw has configured (re-read on every app launch).
#            Picking any other model in a conversation uses that model directly.
#            With the bundled adaptive-model plugin (extensions/adaptive-model),
#            OpenClaw itself runs each message on the chosen model, so every
#            configured model qualifies, including OAuth / auth-profile ones;
#            the router answers only when the plugin cannot decide.
#   fallback otherwise: cloud model primary, local model as its fallback.
#
# The model selection is only changed while it is still the installer's own;
# a model the user picks later is left alone.
#
# LiteLLM is installed on the user's Mac (managed Python + hash-locked
# packages, ~200-300 MB) only in hybrid mode; the build bundles uv plus the
# lock. Both versions must be exact pins. Never use litellm 1.82.7 / 1.82.8
# (the compromised March 2026 PyPI releases); prefer a stable release that has
# been out for at least a week, and >= 1.94 (LLM classifier for
# auto_router/complexity_router).
OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ENABLE_LITELLM=1
OPENCLAW_LITELLM_VERSION=1.102.0
OPENCLAW_UV_VERSION=0.12.8
# OPENCLAW_LITELLM_PYTHON=3.12

# Which configured model serves each non-SIMPLE tier. Candidates are the
# models `openclaw models list` shows whose connection LiteLLM can use
# directly: a models.providers entry with an OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini /
# Ollama API and a plain, ${VAR} or env-SecretRef key. Models whose
# credentials exist only inside OpenClaw (auth profiles, OAuth logins,
# file/exec secrets) stay selectable directly but are not routed to. Unset tiers are chosen automatically: COMPLEX = the cloud
# model above; MEDIUM = a cheaper model (lower configured cost, else a
# "mini/flash/lite..." name); REASONING = a reasoning-capable model; each
# falls back to the cloud model above. Pin with OpenClaw refs, e.g.:
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ROUTER_TIER_MEDIUM=openrouter/openai/gpt-4o-mini
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ROUTER_TIER_COMPLEX=vllm/qwen3-235b
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ROUTER_TIER_REASONING=openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-r1

# Build switches for the three one-click features. Each is 0, 1 or unset, and the same variable in the build
# environment wins over this file (e.g. OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_LLAMA=0 pnpm mac:installer). Unset does NOT mean "on": it
# keeps the old, configuration-driven behaviour (a feature is only on when the keys above for it are filled in).
# Only 1 insists on the feature and fails the build when its keys are missing; only 0 forces it off. None of them changes the Gateway LaunchAgent or the non-interactive onboarding, which
# always run; with the default model off the app's own model picker asks on first launch.
#   DEFAULT_MODEL  0: bake no default online model.  1: require OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_AI_BASE_URL/_MODEL above.
#   LLAMA          0: no llama-server, no local fallback model.  1: require OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_LLAMA_MODEL.
#   LITELLM        0: no LiteLLM router.  1: bundle it (needs OPENCLAW_LITELLM_VERSION and OPENCLAW_UV_VERSION).
#                  Replaces OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_ENABLE_LITELLM, which still works when this is unset. Hybrid routing
#                  needs both the llama fallback and a default model.
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_DEFAULT_MODEL=1
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_LLAMA=1
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_LITELLM=0

# Optional: ship the bundled Nexus Agent Core plugin switched on. With 1, the installed app enables the plugin,
# turns on its feature switches, pins the FAKE demo provider (no real external effect), and appends Nexus' tools to
# tools.alsoAllow (existing entries kept, no duplicates), once per preset version -- so Nexus works in the app right
# after install with no `openclaw config` steps. Anything else (unset, 0) leaves Nexus off, as shipped. The same
# variable in the build environment wins: OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_NEXUS_PRESET=1 pnpm mac:installer
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_NEXUS_PRESET=1
# Switch names to turn on (comma separated, letters only); default shown. vaultEnabled is the personal file vault and
# evidenceBlobsEnabled stores evidence file bytes (bundled plugins may; installs from a tarball may not). Leave either
# out of the list to ship it switched off.
# OPENCLAW_INSTALLER_NEXUS_SWITCHES=tasksEnabled,decisionsEnabled,claimsEnabled,preferencesEnabled,watchersEnabled,vaultEnabled,evidenceBlobsEnabled
